# The Remote's Cut (S-5): Zap's own song. Zap appoints itself the director; every chorus is a cut.

[verse 1]
"I've got a button for the rain" = 0/.5 0/.5 4 4 5 5 4 4/2 | I 4, V 4
"A button for the sun" = 4 5 4 2 1 0/3 | IV 4, I 4
"A button with the label gone" = 0/.5 0/.5 4 4 5 5 4 4/2 | I 4, V 4
"I press it just for fun" = 4 5 4 2 1 0/3 | IV 4, I 4 ; do shrug

[chorus]
"Zap cut to the moon" = 7 7 5 4 4/4 | I 4, IV 4 ; do gasp
"Zap cut to the cake" = 7 7 5 4 2/4 | I 4, V 4
"I don't know where I'm going" = 4/.5 5/.5 7 5 4 5 4/3 | IV 4, I 4
"But I'm sure of each mistake" = 4 5 4 2 1 2 0/2 | II 4, V 2, I 2 ; do nod

[verse 2]
"One more press for luck" = 4 4 5 4 2/4 | I 4, V 4
"Cut to the bright blue sky" = 7 5 4 2 1 0/3 | IV 4, I 4
"Now I'm in the frame" = 4 4 5 4 2/4 | I 4, V 4
"Cut to a sleepy cat" = 7 5 4 2 1 0/3 | IV 4, I 4 ; react laugh

[repeat chorus]
